# Card

The unit of page composition: a bordered surface grouping related
content under an optional title.

<%= embed :card, :playground %>

## When to use

- Grouping related content into a titled section: a record's
  details, a settings group, a chart with its caption.
- Building page grids — cards in a `grid gap-4` are the standard
  page layout (see *Spacing and layout*).

## When not to use

- Around a whole page — the page region is the container; cards
  group within it.
- Nesting — a card inside a card adds border noise without grouping
  anything new; use headings or separators inside one card.
- A single metric — `stat_card` is the purpose-built variant.

## Usage

`render_card` (`Gesso::Components::CardHelper`) renders the bordered surface —
semantic HTML (`<header>` with `<h2>` + description, `<section>` body,
`<footer>`) that basecoat styles directly. The block is the card body.

```erb
<%%= render_card(title: "Patient", description: "NHS number 943 476 5919") do %>
  Card body content
<%% end %>
```

For a richer header — an icon, a badge, a custom layout — pass
pre-rendered markup as `header:` instead of `title`/`description`. Use
`id:` to set the card's id (e.g. for anchor links).

```erb
<%% header = capture do %>
  <div class="flex items-center gap-3">
    <%%= inline_svg_tag "icons/users.svg", class: "size-5 text-primary" %>
    <h2 class="text-lg">Patient details</h2>
  </div>
<%% end %>

<%%= render_card(id: "patient-1234567", header: header) do %>
  Card body content
<%% end %>
```

<%= embed :card, :custom_header %>

| Param | Notes |
| ----- | ----- |
| `title` | optional header heading (default header) |
| `description` | optional sub-text under the title (default header) |
| `header` | pre-rendered header markup; replaces the default title/description header |
| `footer` | optional footer content (text or pre-rendered markup) |
| `id` | optional id on the card element |
| `classes` | extra CSS classes |

## Do and don't

- Do one topic per card; if a card needs two titles, it is two
  cards.
- Do use `description` for the card's one-line purpose rather than a
  paragraph at the top of the body.
- Do prefer `title`/`description` for ordinary cards; reach for the
  `header:` slot only when the header genuinely needs more (an icon, a
  badge, a custom layout).
- Don't reach for `footer` as a button bar by habit — actions
  belong with the content they act on; the footer suits metadata
  and links.
- Don't style card borders/shadows per page — uniform card chrome
  is what makes grids scan.

## Accessibility and content

- The title renders as an `<h2>` inside `<header>` — keep the
  page's heading order in mind (one `<h1>` above, see
  *Typography*).
- Card titles are nouns, sentence case: "Recent contacts", not
  "View your recent contacts here".
